{"availability":"available","full":"guyrotem/google-translate-server","name":"google-translate-server","description":"Google Translate Proxy API","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":99,"forks":33,"created":"2016-10-07T18:44:09Z","updated":"2021-01-03T01:30:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://google-translate-proxy.herokuapp.com/","topics":[],"demo":"https://google-translate-proxy.herokuapp.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:10.717Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:10.717Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T16:12:10.717Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:09.392Z","stars":99,"forks":33},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:10.717Z","stars":99,"forks":33}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Since around December 1st 2020, Google translate started using a newer API version. the older API discussed here still works, BUT:","Fortunately, I kept historical TKK values, so the service is working again (for now), using previously stored values. However, I would no longer not recommend this solution for any purpose.","Can't I just call the API used by Google Translate? Well, sure, just open the networking panel of the Dev tools and see where the requests go. You would notice that the API requires around a dozen parameters, most of which you will quickly understand or walk around them easily. ...except for \"tk\", which has some random-looking values: e.g.: \"258417.372466\". Try to fake it with random values, and you will get HTTP status 403 (Forbidden). It turns out that \"tk\" is a hash value based on your query (the string you wish to translate) and some private key (called TKK), which is embedded in your DOM…"],"features":["new TKK values are no longer available when loading the site.","old TKK values still work, but who knows for how long (or when the old API will be removed completely).","get your hands on some private key (by loading Google Translate website) => tkk","calc: tk := googleHashFunction(query, tkk)","call the AJAX API with (query, tk, targetLang, sourceLang, ...) and some more irrelevant fields"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guyrotem/google-translate-server/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"9aea32e6971bc4fe862832461c014da6e7927121397c622f880e205fd855cbae","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:26:39.267Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:04.267Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2021-01-03T01:30:02Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:04.269Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Since around December 1st 2020, Google translate started using a newer API version. the older API discussed here still works, BUT:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guyrotem/google-translate-server/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"If you need to use it for anything beyond personal usage, please create an enterprise account. (This is presumably why a friendlier API is not supplied by Google).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guyrotem/google-translate-server/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9aea32e6971bc4fe862832461c014da6e7927121397c622f880e205fd855cbae","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guyrotem/google-translate-server/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:04.268Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/guyrotem/google-translate-server/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:04.268Z","hash":"9aea32e6971bc4fe862832461c014da6e7927121397c622f880e205fd855cbae","originalBytes":7264,"storedBytes":7264,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["api","string","google","query","translate","languages","tkk","get","language","may","see","code","postgres","some","values","around","available","create","example","input","longer","multiple","npm","private","queries","sourcelang","target","using","which","array","below","call","case","data","env","here","important","install","iso2","key","letters","ma